[{:seon.task/name "each-run-teaches-the-next"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21 (DECISIONS: every live run better than the last): learn from every attempt automatically, without regressions, slowdown or growth. Found by hand on the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's code (`seon.fences/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded`): 8 turns, 59 errors, no fix; the causes were readable only by querying its branch's evaluation records: `clojure.repl/source` failing for platform vars, `slurp` of repository files not found, guessed namespaces. Extend what exists, add nothing beside it: `seon.learn/waste` already charges an attempt's wasted forms to the context producer that led to them and the judge records it (`:seon.end/waste`, `seon.reconcile/judge-tx`, class `:waste` in `seon.problems`). Make that record answer \"what did this attempt lack\": its failed forms grouped by kind (an unresolved var or namespace, no source, file not found, a contract refusal, a wrong arity), each kind with its count and one example form, and the names it tried to read that its context did not show. Then the live-run comparison: `seon.e2e`'s model runs (`bin/check e2e model ...`, `scenario <k> model`) record their per-task numbers (outcome, turns, model calls, tokens) in the run's kept output, and a run compares itself with the previous run of the same tasks, printing what got worse as a finding (no clock, no threshold invented: worse than last time is the finding). Also: the door's `seon.turn/context-block` passes `:gaps-before` like the turn loop does, so outside agents stop seeing every pre-existing uncontracted function as a contract gap; and the agent's instructions (`seon.context/system-prompt`) name today's verbs (`my.schema/register!`, `source`), each resolving. Budget: about 120 net src lines; no new namespace; nothing added to the turn's hot path beyond the fold that already runs at the attempt's end."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/an-attempt-records-what-it-lacked
                      seon.e2e-test/a-run-reports-what-got-worse-than-the-last
                      seon.context-test/the-door-context-shows-only-new-contract-gaps}}]
